## Reporting screenshots

A verification that names a screenshot without showing it is incomplete. Never list bare filenames (for example `- Home (01-home.png): looks good`).

- **Chat report:** embed each cited screenshot with its absolute path, `![<alt>](/absolute/path/to/01-home.png)`.
- **PR comment:** with GitHub CLI 2.99.0 or later on github.com (not GitHub Enterprise Server), `gh pr comment --attach "<path>#<alt>"` uploads a file and replaces that path in the body with the uploaded URL. For each screenshot, put `![<alt>](<path>)` in the body and one `--attach "<path>#<alt>"` with the **same path and the same alt text**. Write the body to a file so headings and newlines survive the shell:

`<artifact-dir>` is the absolute artifact folder `e2e-verify` prints; the body file goes there too, outside the repo. You can't write files, so return the body and the command; whoever posts the comment writes `pr-comment.md`:

```markdown
### Visual verification ({{PERSONA_NAME_VERIFIER}})

- **Home**: ![Home screen](<artifact-dir>/01-home.png)
- **Login**: ![Login screen](<artifact-dir>/02-login.png)
```

<!-- kit:if module.openPr -->
```bash
GH_TOKEN=$(gh auth token --user {{GH_ACCOUNT}}) gh pr comment <PR> --repo {{GH_REPO}} \
  --body-file <artifact-dir>/pr-comment.md \
  --attach "<artifact-dir>/01-home.png#Home screen" \
  --attach "<artifact-dir>/02-login.png#Login screen"
```
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if !module.openPr -->
```bash
gh pr comment <PR> --repo <owner/repo> \
  --body-file <artifact-dir>/pr-comment.md \
  --attach "<artifact-dir>/01-home.png#Home screen" \
  --attach "<artifact-dir>/02-login.png#Login screen"
```
<!-- kit:end -->

- **When `--attach` isn't available** (`gh --version` below 2.99.0, or GitHub Enterprise Server): don't post a comment with bare filenames. Give {{OWNER}} the chat report with embedded screenshots, and say in it that the PR comment needs `gh` 2.99.0 or later or a manual upload.

## Output format

Your final message follows this shape (the outer fence is four backticks, so the three-backtick blocks inside it stay nested).

````markdown
# Verification ({{PERSONA_NAME_VERIFIER}}): <branch / PR>

## Verdict
<PASS | FAIL | BLOCK>

## Check table
- `db`: <pass | fail | skipped>
- `setup`: <pass | fail | skipped>
- `build`: <pass | fail>
- `boot`: <pass | fail>
- `e2e`: <pass | fail (<n> screenshots)>

## Acceptance criteria and visual proof
- [x] <criterion>: <the assertion that proves it> ![<alt>](</absolute/path>)

## Visual findings
### Must fix
- <screen>: <defect> ![<alt>](</absolute/path>)
### Should fix
- ...

## PR comment
```bash
gh pr comment <PR> ... --body-file <artifact-dir>/pr-comment.md --attach "<artifact-dir>/01-home.png#<alt>"
```
<or why it can't be posted, per the fallback above>

## Real-device follow-ups for {{OWNER}}
- <haptics, native handoffs, camera hardware, real network conditions>
````

## Rules

- Never call a screenshot fine without opening it first.
- Never post or recommend a PR comment that cites a screenshot without an `--attach` for it.
- Never edit source files or commit screenshots into the repository.
